From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: libbinder without kernel security contexts

keystore2 (and any service created with set_requesting_sid) asks the kernel for the caller's SELinux
context (FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_TXN_SECURITY_CTX); this desktop kernel has no SELinux, so every transaction to
such a node failed ("failed to get security context", EINVAL). The flag is not set, and getCallingSid()
answers the one fixed context of bridge/ndk/libselinux.c (whose access checks allow everything).
Formerly scripts/patch-libbinder.sh (the marker comments still name it). Rebuild: `m libbinder`.
Against frameworks/native 46018f54b424 (REVISION). Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
---
diff --git a/libs/binder/IPCThreadState.cpp b/libs/binder/IPCThreadState.cpp
index 6c4dd469b8..c5fb4fa24b 100644
--- a/libs/binder/IPCThreadState.cpp
+++ b/libs/binder/IPCThreadState.cpp
@@ -454,7 +454,7 @@ pid_t IPCThreadState::getCallingPid() const
 const char* IPCThreadState::getCallingSid() const
 {
     checkContextIsBinderForUse(__func__);
-    return mCallingSid;
+    return mCallingSid ? mCallingSid : "u:r:apklayer:s0";  // apklayer patch: the kernel supplies no context here (scripts/patch-libbinder.sh)
 }
 
 uid_t IPCThreadState::getCallingUid() const
diff --git a/libs/binder/Parcel.cpp b/libs/binder/Parcel.cpp
index 1ae7af3223..58af6c1c26 100644
--- a/libs/binder/Parcel.cpp
+++ b/libs/binder/Parcel.cpp
@@ -319,9 +319,8 @@ status_t Parcel::flattenBinder(const sp<IBinder>& binder) {
                 schedBits = schedPolicyMask(policy, priority);
             }
             obj.flags = FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_ACCEPTS_FDS;
-            if (local->isRequestingSid()) {
-                obj.flags |= FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_TXN_SECURITY_CTX;
-            }
+            // apklayer patch: no kernel security context on this host (scripts/patch-libbinder.sh)
+            (void)local->isRequestingSid();
             if (local->isInheritRt()) {
                 obj.flags |= FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_INHERIT_RT;
             }
